Key Concepts & Operations Covered

Distinct Elements (distinct()): Removing duplicate items from collections.

Sorting (sorted()): Sorting elements in natural order or using custom comparators (ascending and descending).

String Aggregation (Collectors.joining()): Concatenating stream strings with delimiters, prefixes, and suffixes.

Min / Max Selection (min(), max()): Finding boundary elements using custom comparators.

Element Existence Checks:

anyMatch(): Checks if at least one element matches a predicate.

allMatch(): Checks if all elements satisfy a predicate.

noneMatch(): Checks if no elements satisfy a predicate.

Skipping & Limiting:

limit(n): Truncating the stream to a maximum size.

skip(n): Discarding the first n elements.

Target Audience & Goal

Aimed at solidifying foundational stream skills with real-world scenarios like deduplication, custom sorting, and matching validation.